# English-only texts

Everything the model or a developer reads in this repo is English:

- system prompts, nudges, guardrail/oracle notes, tool results and markers (`…[clipped: …]`, `(already in context …)`)
- skills and rules (`extensions/codeforge/resources/**`, `governance/builtins.ts`)
- status/activity labels, reports (`BUGS.md`, plan report), READMEs, `HEURISTICS.md`
- benchmark prompts (`task.json`) and fixture docs/cards (`Depends on:`, `Acceptance criteria`)

Portuguese is allowed only in **matchers of user input** (regexes, skill `triggers`, stopwords), because users write in Portuguese:

```ts
// ✅ matcher — keeps recognizing Portuguese requests
/\b(review|revis\w*|encontr\w* (os )?bugs?)\b/i
// ❌ text sent to the model
`…[cortado: mostradas linhas 1-${n}]`
// ✅
`…[clipped: showing lines 1-${n} of ${total}]`
```

Chat replies to the user follow the user's language; this rule is about files in the repo.
